<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 07_colors/19: System colours -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>System colours</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .system { color-scheme: light dark; background: Canvas; color: CanvasText; border: 2px solid ButtonBorder; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; }
    .system a { color: LinkText; }
    .system button { background: ButtonFace; color: ButtonText; border: 1px solid ButtonBorder; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; }
    .system mark { background: Mark; color: MarkText; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>System colours</h1>
    <p class="lead">Canvas, CanvasText and friends follow the user's colour scheme.</p>
    <section class="system">
      <p>This panel uses system colours: switch your operating system to dark mode and it follows.</p>
      <p><a href="#x">A link</a> and <mark>marked text</mark>.</p>
      <button type="button">A button</button>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
